Josh's total investment is $80,000 (purchase) + $50,000 (repairs) = $130,000.

The house's value increased by 150% of its original purchase price, so the new value is:
$80,000 + (150% of $80,000) = $80,000 + $120,000 = $200,000.

Profit = New value - Total investment = $200,000 - $130,000 = $70,000.

#### 70000 [end of text]


